## Sanitizer policy

| Model     | Parameter          | Action                                                                                         |
| --------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `glm-5.2` | `thinking`         | Set `{type: "enabled"}` when reasoning is requested, else `{type: "disabled"}`                 |
| `glm-5.2` | `reasoning_effort` | Normalized via `normalizeZaiEffort()` → `off`↦off (thinking disabled), `low`/`medium`↦high, `high` pass-through, `xhigh`↦max |
| `glm-4.7` | `thinking`         | Set `{type: "enabled"|"disabled"}`; no reasoning_effort support                                |
| `glm-4.7` | `reasoning_effort` | Deleted                                                                                        |

Apply `PolicyZai` case in `applyThinkingPolicy()` and `stripUnsupportedParams()`.

## Reasoning effort normalization (Z.AI-specific)

Z.AI accepts `reasoning_effort` values: `none`, `minimal`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `max`.
The gateway normalizes higher-level effort labels **down to what the catalog
advertises** via `normalizeZaiEffort()` (only `off`, `high`, `max` are ever sent):

| UI label        | Sent to Z.AI |
| --------------- | ------------ |
| Off / None      | `off` (thinking disabled) |
| Low             | `high`  |
| Medium          | `high`  |
| High            | `high`  |
| XHigh / Max     | `max`  |

The `ReasoningEffortCatalog` entry for `glm-5.2` advertises: `Off`, `high`, `max`.
`glm-4.7` does not appear in the catalog (no effort selection).

