## Balance API

Z.AI is credits-based (GLM Coding Plan). The usage dashboard fetches remaining
credits via the quota API:
- `GET https://api.z.ai/api/monitor/usage/quota/limit` (Bearer auth, returns `data.limits[]` buckets of type `CREDIT_LIMIT` with `remaining`/`percentage`). The weekly bucket carries a `nextResetTime`; the 5-hour bucket does not.

Also checkable manually at https://z.ai/manage-apikey/billing.

## Symptoms & fixes

### `vision_call_failed with 429 "Insufficient balance"`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ----- | ---- | ----- |
| Vision describer logs `vision_call_failed` with status 429 and body `"Insufficient balance or no resource package. Please recharge."` | The vision describer is hitting the on-demand endpoint (`/api/paas/v4`) but the Z.AI key is a GLM Coding Plan key — these are separate billing buckets and the on-demand bucket has no balance | Use the coding-plan endpoint (`/api/coding/paas/v4`) for `glm-4.6v` vision calls. `glm-4.6v` is available on the Coding Plan (see https://docs.z.ai/devpack/overview under "Credit Calculation" → GLM-4.6V（Vision MCP）). The vision describer in `server.go` now uses `ChatCompletionsURL(config.ProviderZai)` which resolves to the coding-plan base URL. |

### `Z.AI request fails with Unauthorized`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ----- | ---- | ----- |
| Z.AI returns 401 or "Unauthorized" even with valid API key | Using wrong API endpoint for the user's plan type (e.g., on-demand API `/api/paas/v4` vs GLM Coding Plan API `/api/coding/paas/v4`) | Verify the user's Z.AI plan type (Coding Plan vs on-demand). For GLM Coding Plan, use `https://api.z.ai/api/coding/paas/v4`. For on-demand, use `https://api.z.ai/api/paas/v4`. |

### `Z.AI request appears to hang or timeout`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ----- | ---- | ----- |
| Cursor request to Z.AI model appears to hang for over a minute with no response and no credits used | Z.AI GLM Coding Plan has higher latency (~5s to first token) than other providers (e.g., DeepSeek). Gateway proxy works fine (verify via curl to loopback), but Cursor client may timeout before first token arrives. | Verify gateway proxy works via direct curl test. If successful, inform user that Z.AI has higher latency and the "hang" may be Cursor-side timeout. No gateway fix required. |

